m5f|v|To draw off by degrees; to cause to flow gradually out or off; hence, to cause the exhaustion of. ; To exhaust of liquid contents by drawing them off; to make gradually dry or empty; to remove surface water, as from streets, by gutters, etc.; to deprive of moisture; hence, to exhaust; to empty of wealth, resources, or the like; as, to drain a country of its specie. ; To filter. ; To flow gradually; as, the water of low ground drains off. ; To become emptied of liquor by flowing or dropping; as, let the vessel stand and drain.	o:ak6,17,1;6ks,4,6;tl5,1,2~6ks,4,6;tl5,1,2;ak6,17,1	s:1xez,61,2;6kq,37,5;m5f,18,1~6kq,37,5;1xez,61,2;m5f,18,1	d:1o2v,29,3;1vfv,21,4;1nkg,10,5;bn6,10,5;tmw,8,5;ugr,4,4;e9a,4,7~e9a,4,7;1nkg,10,5;tmw,8,5;bn6,10,5;1vfv,21,4;ugr,4,4;1o2v,29,3	D:1nkg,10,5;r4l,9,4;1vcq,2,3;1w24,2,2~1nkg,10,5;r4l,9,4;1vcq,2,3;1w24,2,2
