m5s|n|A composition, in prose or poetry, accommodated to action, and intended to exhibit a picture of human life, or to depict a series of grave or humorous actions of more than ordinary interest, tending toward some striking result. It is commonly designed to be spoken and represented by actors on the stage. ; A series of real events invested with a dramatic unity and interest. ; Dramatic composition and the literature pertaining to or illustrating it; dramatic literature.	a:1qwk,90,1;1jz0,68,3;238u,51,1;soq,50,1;tsa,27,3;15u7,26,6;28qm,26,3;7md,25,3;16i4,23,4;1b5y,15,7;1w1v,10,14~1w1v,10,14;1b5y,15,7;15u7,26,6;16i4,23,4;7md,25,3;28qm,26,3;tsa,27,3;1jz0,68,3;1qwk,90,1;soq,50,1;238u,51,1	v:238u,51,1;soq,50,1;bag,30,4~bag,30,4;soq,50,1;238u,51,1	V:dbk,59,1;izx,44,3~izx,44,3;dbk,59,1	n:dyw,111,5;wj,47,8;1isl,34,2;290l,6,4~wj,47,8;dyw,111,5;290l,6,4;1isl,34,2	N:1nhp,84,2;dbk,79,4;372,56,5;1tqi,55,7~1tqi,55,7;372,56,5;dbk,79,4;1nhp,84,2
