mf1|n|An instrument of percussion, consisting either of a hollow cylinder, over each end of which is stretched a piece of skin or vellum, to be beaten with a stick; or of a metallic hemisphere (kettledrum) with a single piece of skin to be so beaten; the common instrument for marking time in martial music; one of the pair of tympani in an orchestra, or cavalry band. ; Anything resembling a drum in form ; A sheet iron radiator, often in the shape of a drum, for warming an apartment by means of heat received from a stovepipe, or a cylindrical receiver for steam, etc. ; A small cylindrical box in which figs, etc., are packed. ; The tympanum of the ear; -- often, but incorrectly, applied to the tympanic membrane. ; One of the cylindrical, or nearly cylindrical, blocks, of which the shaft of a column is composed; also, a vertical wall, whether circular or polygonal in plan, carrying a cupola or dome. ; A cylinder on a revolving shaft, generally for the purpose of driving several pulleys, by means of belts or straps passing around its periphery; also, the barrel of a hoisting machine, on which the rope or chain is wound. ; See Drumfish. ; A noisy, tumultuous assembly of fashionable people at a private house; a rout. ; A tea party; a kettledrum.	a:1vnm,126,3;28vc,80,1;14df,61,2;18k8,48,4;1oa1,45,3;1obl,40,6;1udo,24,5;1oab,16,3;16i4,14,4;1dub,12,4~1obl,40,6;1udo,24,5;16i4,14,4;1dub,12,4;18k8,48,4;1oab,16,3;1oa1,45,3;1vnm,126,3;14df,61,2;28vc,80,1	v:1r2j,52,3;mrn,50,1~1r2j,52,3;mrn,50,1	V:6oy,83,11;8yh,42,8;1qw7,37,3~6oy,83,11;8yh,42,8;1qw7,37,3	n:1vnm,120,2;6hx,93,5;u0b,90,3;9v6,88,4;20oy,81,4;28vc,80,1;mrn,78,7;yxx,62,6;8yh,35,5;7yj,20,4;tgm,20,2;1obl,14,1;ici,10,4~mrn,78,7;yxx,62,6;6hx,93,5;8yh,35,5;20oy,81,4;7yj,20,4;9v6,88,4;ici,10,4;u0b,90,3;1vnm,120,2;tgm,20,2;1obl,14,1;28vc,80,1	N:1kq7,94,2;13d1,84,9;6oy,74,6;14gh,68,2;17eu,64,2;1qw7,59,14;14id,57,5;1uc7,51,2;1fq8,51,5;8yh,38,6;230r,35,5;m4o,27,3;17ay,23,10;1w9r,22,5;1adk,21,3~1qw7,59,14;17ay,23,10;13d1,84,9;8yh,38,6